Add NVIDIA NVENC (h264_nvenc) H264 encoder for KPipeWire 6.8.3

On NVIDIA the VAAPI driver is decode-only, so H264VAAPIEncoder cannot
encode and KPipeWire falls back to CPU libx264. Add H264NvencEncoder,
which uses a zero-copy GPU pipeline when an NVIDIA EGL/CUDA render node
is available: DMA-BUF frames are imported via EGLImage, converted to
BT.709 NV12 (full or limited range, padded to even dimensions) in OpenGL,
copied VRAM-to-VRAM into a pooled AV_PIX_FMT_CUDA frame via CUDA-GL
interop (libcuda.so.1 loaded dynamically), and encoded directly by
h264_nvenc with zero PCIe round-trip or CPU swscale.

Falls back cleanly to a pooled single-pass NV12 software path when GPU
interop is unavailable (or KPIPEWIRE_NVENC_NO_ZEROCOPY=1 is set).

Also configures h264_nvenc with explicit profile, zero-latency options
(zerolatency=1, delay=0, multipass=disabled, surfaces=8) for Speed and
NoPreference, fixes sub-millisecond frame pacing in PipeWireProduce, and
fixes lost condition-variable wakeups in PipeWireProduce worker threads.

Tried before the VAAPI path; force with KPIPEWIRE_FORCE_ENCODER=h264_nvenc.

